# Network panel: one label/value pair a row when the card is squeezed. The
# details under the network's name (ping, packet loss, transfer, IP address,
# gateway) are a four-column grid, two pairs a row, sized for the card's 380
# px. On a screen narrower than that the card gets less (about 340 px on a
# Pixel 9a upright), and an IPv4 address ran into its label ("IP
# Address192.168…"). When the card is narrower than it asks for, the grid
# takes two columns, one pair a row; at full width it is as before. Candidate
# for upstream Omarchy.
#
# Against Omarchy 4.5.0-3.

diff --git i/shell/plugins/panels/network/Panel.qml w/shell/plugins/panels/network/Panel.qml
--- i/shell/plugins/panels/network/Panel.qml
+++ w/shell/plugins/panels/network/Panel.qml
@@ -1391,7 +1391,10 @@
 
         GridLayout {
           width: parent.width
-          columns: 4
+          // Two label/value pairs a row while the card has its full width;
+          // one pair a row when a narrow screen squeezes it, so an address
+          // doesn't run into its label.
+          columns: panel.contentWidth < Style.space(380) ? 2 : 4
           columnSpacing: Style.space(20)
           rowSpacing: Style.spacing.labelGap
 
